From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Murgola <andy@murgo.la>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 09:37:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] moe: lock a RAM tier of host experts (--moe-ram-mib)

Locks up to N MiB of the host expert slices in RAM at context creation
(VirtualLock / mlock after a ranged prefetch, a few layers at a time): the
most used experts of the profile first, skipping the ones the device cache
already holds, else from the first layer on. Neither a prompt scan nor another
process can page them out, so their misses from the device cache come at
memcpy speed instead of the soft-fault or SSD path.
